t takes 11 ticks to go beyond 100%, so the target first sits above 100% at 11 s, and the first comparison against it is the 12th tick.

The target after n raises is 0.9 × 1.01ⁿ, and n = ln(1/0.9) / ln(1.01) ≈ 10.6 raises to reach 100%. Since raises are whole ticks, that rounds up to 11.

Tick (seconds)	Target compared	% of max
1	0.9 × 1.01⁰	90.0%
10	0.9 × 1.01⁹	98.4%
11	0.9 × 1.01¹⁰	99.4% (raised to 100.4% after this tick)
12	0.9 × 1.01¹¹	100.4%
At tick 12 the target is 100.4% of the max. Even a node running exactly at max throughput fails it (the check is throughput <= target), so nobody survives past 12 s. Your observed throughput sits at ~99.95% of the max (271.7 vs 271.8), which is why the trigger fired at exactly the 12th tick.

